text It can either be an anchor tag <a> or a <div>, as a direct child of either:
text navbar
text navbar-brand
text navbar-start
text navbar-end
text navbar-dropdown
text You can add the following modifier classes:
text is-expanded to turn it into a full-width element
text is-tab to add a bottom border on hover and show the bottom border using is-active
h3 "Transparent navbar #"
text To seamlessly integrate the navbar in any visual context, you can add the is-transparent modifier on the navbar component. This will remove any hover or active background from the navbar items.
text Example
row
  link "https://bulma.io" https://bulma.io
  row
    row
      link Home https://bulma.io/
      row
        link Docs https://bulma.io/documentation/overview/start/
        col
          link Overview https://bulma.io/documentation/overview/start/
          link Modifiers https://bulma.io/documentation/overview/modifiers/
          link Columns https://bulma.io/documentation/columns/basics/
